cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this playbook or the job script, please cite it as below."
title: "MyQ Mono Job Redirect: reserving a colour MFP for colour documents with a server side MyQ X job script"
abstract: >-
  A production deployment playbook and PHP job script for MyQ X 10.2 that
  reserves a colour multifunction printer for colour documents. The script runs
  as an "Actions after processing" rule on a Pull Print queue: when the MyQ Job
  Parser reports zero colour pages, the job is relocated with moveToQueue() to a
  parallel queue containing the same printers minus the colour device, so a mono
  job simply has no opportunity to be released there. Nothing changes on any user
  workstation, no driver, share, port or GPO is touched, and no job is ever
  deleted or duplicated. Five branches are evaluated per job and four of them
  deliberately do nothing, so unreadable content and rights mismatches produce a
  log line rather than a stranded job. An $ENFORCE flag provides a genuine dry
  run against live traffic, and rollback is clearing a single text field with no
  service restart and no downtime. Verified in production on Ricoh IM C2010 and
  IM 2500; the mechanism is server side and device agnostic. Includes a six phase
  runbook, rollback scenarios, limitations, and troubleshooting.
